  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a Duo user, I want the app to fill the cover screen, so that there is no black band.\n\n### Scope\n\nFilling the cover screen is a fix, not an evolution: option (a), **M4**. The layouts and the continuity across folds (LOT-147, LOT-145) go to M5. The legacy side is the track of PR #372 (check #373).\n\n- Milestone: **M4** (operator decisions of 2026-11-02 on [#379](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/379): UXD-25 (cover screen)). Follow-up of LOT-082 (#100), 147 (#237, M5). GAP 215, 216, 217 in `docs/migration/GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md`.\n- Module: App · Difficulty: easy · Priority: medium · a small (a) item (a port of the legacy behaviour), not an evolution.\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master` @ 2440d79): the GAP rows above cite the files and symbols. Tracked by [#413](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/413).\n\n### Depends on\n\n- the merged lots above (done)\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The behaviour matches the legacy app at 2440d79 (cited in the PR), and nothing else changes.\n- [ ] View logic lives in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing in `App/SwiftHFRTests/`; each new test is shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] `xcodebuild build test` green on the iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0), and the `App build + tests` CI job green.\n- [ ] UI strings in French; light, dark and Dynamic Type XL checked; no new dependency; no HFR fact without a source.\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, App/README.md and the spec of the lots above. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Refs`/`Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; the app code starts with the `// Port of … @ 2440d79` comment (AGENTS.md §4).\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
