   "body": "Mac check, session mac/m2-lead. Build: dev-swift 13bb2639 (LOT-185 and LOT-186 merged), iPhone Duo simulator (iOS 27.2, device type iPhone19,4), logged out, no account data.\n\n- ✅ Cover screen, cold launch: the launch screen and the first screen (Drapeaux, with the tab bar and the \"...\" button) fill the whole 1398x2034 display. No black band, no letterboxing. Same result as the legacy track (#372, row 4).\n- ✅ System bars: the status bar, the tab bar and the \"...\" button sit in the vertical strip on the right edge, drawn by the system (HIG \"Designing for iPhone Duo\"); the content fills the rest.\n- ⚪ Inner display, every fold pose, rotation of the cover screen: NOT TESTED. The Duo simulator boots closed, the inner display stays black, and there is no fold control or API (same limit as #372). Needs the physical device.\n- ⚪ `OrientationPolicy` (iPhone idiom: `.allButUpsideDown`, or `.portrait` when rotation is locked): code read only; the simulator does not rotate the cover screen (#372, row 6), so the lock cannot be observed. Needs the device.\n- Project settings read: `INFOPLIST_KEY_UILaunchScreen_Generation = YES`, scene manifest generated, no `UIRequiresFullScreen`, no fixed window size. Nothing in them would cause a band.\n\nI found no cause to fix in the project or scene settings: the band of #368 G.1 does not reproduce on the simulator at this head, so no PR is opened. The remaining question is for the physical Duo (cover and inner display, each pose).",
